{
 "atom": "cli/atoms/std-orb-lint-fetch-deliver.lolo",
 "trait": "OrbLintFetchDeliver",
 "note": "Cases built from the option checks of entities/fetch_deliver.rs: `deliver: ids` with `include` (ORB_FETCH_DELIVER_IDS_ENTITY_REFS) and without a non-empty `emit.success` (ORB_FETCH_DELIVER_IDS_NO_SUCCESS), each program lowered from an .orb fixture and the expected findings the ones `orb validate --json` reports. The controls are rows delivery and a fetch below an unknown head; an empty success and a failure-only emit count as no success, and a fetch inside an object is not found (the Rust walk descends arrays only). ORB_FETCH_DELIVER_IDS_ROWS_READ and ORB_FETCH_TOTAL_NONE_READ are not part of the rule.",
